 34SI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34SI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34SI2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34SI c  2019Li41: {+34}Mg and {+34}Al ions were produced via fragmentation     
 34SI2c  reactions induced by a 1.4-GeV pulsed proton beam from the Proton      
 34SI3c  Synchrotron Booster on a UC{-x} target at ISOLDE-CERN. Th atoms that   
 34SI4c  diffused out of the target matrix were selectively laser ionized using 
 34SI5c  the resonance ionization laser ion source (RILIS) and accelerated to 40
 34SI6c  keV. A=34 nuclei were selected by the ISOLDE General Purpose Separator 
 34SI7c  and implanted onto a movable tape located at the center of the ISOLDE  
 34SI8c  Decay station. The {+34}Mg beam rate is 700 pps {I1} and the {+34}Al   
 34SI9c  beam rate is 800 pps {I1}, both with purities of >99%. |b particles    
 34SIAc  were detected using a 3-cm-thick NE102 plastic scintillator with an    
 34SIBc  efficiency of 90% {I5}. |g rays were detected using five HPGe clover   
 34SICc  detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, |b|g|g-coin, and              
 34SIDc  |be{++}/e{+-}coin. Deduced levels, isomer, J, |p, decay branching      
 34SIEc  ratios, log {Ift}, T{-1/2} and %|b{+-}n of parent, and configuration   
 34SIFc  mixings. Comparisons with large-scale shell-model calculations using   
 34SIGc  the SDPF-U-MIX interaction.                                            
 34AL c  2017Ha23, 2017Ha34: a 69.2-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar primary beam was        
 34AL2c  produced by the Sector Focusing Cyclotron and Separated Sector         
 34AL3c  Cyclotron at the Heavy Ion Research Facility in Lanzhou (HIRFL). The   
 34AL4c  secondary beam containing {+34}Al was produced via the projectile      
 34AL5c  fragmentation of {+40}Ca impinging on a 182.6-mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be target  
 34AL6c  and was selected using |DE-tof-B|r by the Radioactive Ion Beam Line in 
 34AL7c  Lanzhou (RIBLL). The secondary beam ions were transported into a target
 34AL8c  chamber filled with low-temperature nitrogen and implanted into a      
 34AL9c  1500-|mm-thick DSSD sandwiched between two 3000-|mm-thick plastic      
 34ALAc  scintillators for beam diagnostics and veto, respectively. |g rays were
 34ALBc  detected using two Ge clover detectors. The fast timing signals of the 
 34ALCc  |g rays were provided by a lanthanum bromide (LaBr{-3}) detector.      
 34ALDc  Neutrons were detected using two plastic scintillator arrays. Measured 
 34ALEc  implant-|b correlation, E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, |g|g-coin, and |bn-coin.  
 34ALFc  Deduced levels, J, |p, decay branching ratios, log {Ift}, parent       
 34ALGc  {+34}Al and {+34}Al isomer T{-1/2}. Comparisons with shell-model       
 34ALHc  calculations using Gogny D1S and SDPF-M interactions. Also see 2019Wa38
 34ALIc  for the same experiment with 35Al |b-delayed neutron data.             
